1
00:00:00,114 --> 00:00:01,187
Step three.

2
00:00:01,392 --> 00:00:03,943
QueueForge starts the background work.

3
00:00:04,148 --> 00:00:07,864
The first attempt fails, but it remains visible.

4
00:00:08,082 --> 00:00:12,565
QueueForge tries again, and the second attempt succeeds.

5
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:17,253
It creates a signed receipt so the completed result can be verified,

6
00:00:17,457 --> 00:00:18,574
then delivers it.

7
00:00:18,778 --> 00:00:23,203
In Delivery connections, the administrator searches Expense review

8
00:00:23,253 --> 00:00:25,449
and finds the matching send.

9
00:00:25,668 --> 00:00:28,986
The delivery record confirms it was accepted,

10
00:00:29,176 --> 00:00:32,821
and Omar's request now reads Completed.
